---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { identity } from '../data/identity';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy — Adrian Rusu"
  description="How this portfolio handles optional Google Analytics, your locally saved consent preference, and contact links. Change your analytics choice at any time."
>
  <section class="page-intro container">
    <span class="eyebrow">YOUR CHOICE</span>
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p class="intro-description">
      This portfolio has no advertising. I do not sell visitor information. Optional analytics helps
      me understand how people find and use my work.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="section container privacy-content">
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>Optional Google Analytics</h2>
      <p>
        Google Analytics loads only when you choose “Allow analytics.” If you decline, this site
        does not load the Google Analytics tag or send it analytics requests. Advertising storage,
        advertising personalization and Google Signals are disabled.
      </p>
      <p>
        When allowed, Google Analytics can measure page views, broad traffic sources, device and
        browser information, and interactions with the portfolio. It uses first-party cookies to
        help distinguish visits. Google processes this information under its <a
          href="https://policies.google.com/privacy"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer">privacy policy</a
        >.
      </p>
      <h2>What this portfolio measures</h2>
      <p>
        The site records clicks on email, LinkedIn, the résumé PDF and public project source links
        after you allow analytics. These custom events include the public page path and, for project
        links, the project name used in its URL. They do not include your email address, message
        text, full link text, or URL query strings and fragments.
      </p>
      <p>
        Google Analytics may also record standard engagement, outbound-click and file-download
        events according to the property's settings. The named portfolio events distinguish useful
        actions from those general measurements.
      </p>
      <h2>Your analytics preference</h2>
      <p>
        Your choice is saved in this browser's local storage as <code>ar_analytics_consent</code>.
        It is not an account-wide setting. You can allow or decline analytics at any time using the
        settings control below or in the footer.
      </p>
      <p>
        Withdrawing consent disables tracking, removes this site's accessible Google Analytics
        cookies and reloads the page without the tag. This stops future collection from this
        browser; it does not erase information already sent to Google. Clearing browser storage
        removes your saved choice.
      </p>
      <button
        class="privacy-settings"
        type="button"
        data-analytics-settings
        aria-controls="analytics-consent"
        aria-expanded="false">Analytics settings</button
      >
      <noscript
        ><p>
          JavaScript is disabled, so Google Analytics does not load and no analytics preference is
          needed.
        </p></noscript
      >
      <h2>Cloudflare Web Analytics</h2>
      <p>
        Cloudflare Web Analytics is a separate service for aggregate traffic and performance
        measurement. I have not confirmed active collection on this site, and this portfolio does
        not add its tracking script. It is not controlled by the optional Google Analytics
        preference.
      </p>
      <h2>Fonts and external links</h2>
      <p>
        This site currently loads its fonts from Google Fonts, independently of the analytics
        choice. Following a link to GitHub, LinkedIn or another website takes you to a service with
        its own privacy practices. Email links open your email application.
      </p>
      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        For questions about this portfolio or its analytics, email <a
          href={`mailto:${identity.email}`}>{identity.email}</a
        >.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
<style>
  .privacy-content {
    padding-top: 0;
  }
  .prose {
    max-width: 760px;
  }
  .privacy-settings {
    padding: 0.65rem 1rem;
    min-height: 44px;
    border: 1px solid var(--accent-light);
    border-radius: 4px;
    background: var(--surface);
    cursor: pointer;
    margin-block: 1rem;
  }
</style>
